From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:02:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 26/52] Show an outline of the headings next to a Markdown file

View menu "Outline" (Ctrl+Alt+O; config markdown_outline, off by default)
shows a narrow panel left of the Markdown tab with its headings: ATX,
setext and the <h1>..<h6> of HTML blocks, indented by level, none from
code blocks. The heading above the cursor is highlighted. A click puts
the cursor on the heading and scrolls it to the top of the editor and,
when the preview shows, of the preview. Headings are read with the
existing reparse debounce, also in Source view while the outline is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

